# What `docker build` must NOT send to the daemon.
#
# The checkout is 1.2 GB and the wheel needs about a tenth of it. Without this
# file every build -- local and CI -- copies docs (651 MB, published from
# docs/source by the docs workflow and never part of a wheel), tools (383 MB,
# mostly tutorial capture media), tests and the feature ledger into the build
# context before the first instruction runs.
#
# DENY-LIST, NOT AN ALLOW-LIST, on purpose. `pip install .` reads more of the
# root than is obvious -- setup.py opens README.rst, pyproject.toml carries the
# metadata, and setup.py's `data_files` installs packaging/linux's .desktop
# file and its eight icon sizes on Linux. An allow-list that forgets one of
# those fails at build time with a message about the wrong thing.
#
# Everything named here is excluded from the WHEEL as well, either because it
# sits outside the `spacr` package or because MANIFEST.in prunes it; so
# nothing below can change what the image contains.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude/

docs/
tools/
tests/
features/
Notebooks/
proposals/
measurements/
spaCR_settings/
spacr_drivers/
data/
conda-forge/
settings/
rtd_trigger.txt

# 90 home-screen renders the maintainer chooses from, 13 MB, pruned from the
# distribution by MANIFEST.in.
spacr/resources/home/
spacr/resources/icons/backup_icons/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# The images themselves: a stale build output must never become build input.
**/*.whl
**/*.tar.gz
